> The 2nd entry in the Early Strategy Series for Newbies.
> How do you handle fountains in general?  Do you pass
> them up early on or kick/quaff them?

I don't quaff from sinks until I can handle the worst
outcome.  Since it can be the worst potion that is
after I've done the Quest and Castle.  Also the sick
can turn into a fountain that get can curse random
items so I hesitate until I have an uncurse method.

I don't kick sinks until I can handle the types of
monsters that come out of sinks.  Foocubi mean I wait
until I have high enough charisma that I know I can
get a benefit not a problem from an encounter, also
Quest range of strength.  But fighting foocubi or
puddings could be done at about the strength it takes
to handle Medusa.

So I note the levels that have sinks and come back
after facing Medusa.

> Drop rings down them?  At what point do you do this?

Sinks can only produce one ring but they will eat
infinite rings.  In general I'm only willing to lose
a ring if I have more than one of the same type.
Rings are very high on my ID priority list so I
will only use a sink if I have more than one of some
type, and then I will kick the sink until it gives me
a ring before dropping my duplicate ring.  Since
kicking the sink creates monsters, I only do it after
handling Medusa.

Like fountains, sinks are a trick put into the game
to sucker early characters into getting killed. ;^)


